A class in Java is a blueprint or template used to create objects. It defines the properties and behaviours of an object using variables and methods. For example, Student is a class that can contain student details like ID, name and methods like study or display."
The commonly discussed types are:
-----------------------------------
1. Concrete class
2. Abstract class
3. Final class
4. Static nested class
5. Inner class
6. Anonymous inner class
7. Local inner class
