Functions in Java
A function in Java is a block of code that performs a specific task whenever it is called.
*No arguments and no return value
*Arguments and no return value
*No arguments and return value
*Arguments and return value
class Thishi {
    int Thishitha(int a, int b) {
        return a * b;
    }
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Thishi obj = new Thishi();
        int result = obj.Thishitha(10, 20);
        System.out.println("Multiplication = " + result);
    }
}

